{"id": "unknown-2026-11-21-009", "date": "2026-11-21", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Japan’s steel exports may fall to lowest level since 1999 in 2026", "content": "<p>Japan’s steel exports could fall below 29 million tonnes in 2026, the lowest level since 1999, when shipments totaled 28 million tonnes, reports BigMint, citing Japan Metal Daily. According to Japan’s Ministry of Finance, steel product exports in October decreased by 16.1% y/y to 2.11 million tonnes. Total shipments in January–October reached about 23.4 million [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://gmk.center/en/news/japan-s-steel-exports-may-fall-to-lowest-level-since-1999-in-2026/\" dat", "sources": [{"name": "gmk_center", "url": "https://gmk.center/en/news/japan-s-steel-exports-may-fall-to-lowest-level-since-1999-in-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
